/// The transplant fixture: one artifact, two hostings, one transcript. It is
/// driven by the wasmtime harness and by the browser suite from a shared
/// script, and is instantiated by no deployment configuration — it is declared
/// here because it ships in the surface asset tree, and a shipped kind owns an
/// authored specification.
///
/// The guest is deliberately input-agnostic: it iterates whatever input windows
/// the host binds and summarizes each one, so no input port is load-bearing for
/// it. Every input is therefore optional, and the ones named here are the ones
/// the harnesses bind — a deployment that bound none of them would still get a
/// well-formed transcript.
///
/// `sampled` is the port a host conformance run binds at `push_depth = 0`: a
/// window that is context only and never wakes its owner. The guest treats it
/// like any other input, so what the port proves is the host's gate, not the
/// guest's.
///
/// `tick` is the self-publish chain: the guest parks its next tick on it when
/// the port's deferred window is empty and config names `tick_ms`, so a
/// standing tick is re-armed exactly once however many activations see it.
///
/// `out` and `report` are not optional. Every activation publishes its
/// activation report on `report`; `out` carries the echo markers and is the
/// only port the deferral markers park, cancel, and edit on. Bodies are
/// free-form (a JSON report, echo markers), so no port carries a doctype.
component ProcessorTransplant {
  abi = processor;
  requires = [ports, log, config];
  optional in in;
  optional in ctx;
  optional in sampled;
  optional io tick;
  out out;
  out report;
}
